  "text": "Skip to content\n\nCOMPLIMENTARY SHIPPING ON ORDERS OVER $150\n\nHOME\nCATALOG\nCONTACT\nSartorial Archive\n\nCATALOGUE I / THE HOUSE\n\nObjects with a remembered life\n\nA collection shaped by provenance, handwork and time.\n\nENTER THE CATALOGUE\nRESTORED SELECTION\n\nINDEX II / PROVENANCE\n\n“\nWhat endures carries the record of how it was made.\n\nThe catalogue follows each garment from runway provenance to workshop restoration and permanent archive entry.\n\nREAD ARCHIVE NOTES\n\nPLATE IV / ACCESSION 1957.34.1\n\nFOUNDED\nA continuing workshop tradition since 1987\n01\nORIGIN\nAcquired from private estates in Paris & Antwerp\n02\nMAKER\nNamed and catalogued with every object\n03\nRECORD\nNumbered museum-grade accession certificate\n04\nPIECE NO. 01/12 RESTORED\nRUNWAY 1989–1999 PERMANENT ARCHIVE\nMUSEUM GRADE CONSERVATION\nPRIVATE APPOINTMENTS IN MILAN & PARIS\nPIECE NO. 01/12 RESTORED\nRUNWAY 1989–1999 PERMANENT ARCHIVE\nMUSEUM GRADE CONSERVATION\nPRIVATE APPOINTMENTS IN MILAN & PARIS\nPause editorial highlights\n\nCATALOGUE III / OBJECTS\n\nEntries from the permanent record\n[01]\nCURRENT CATALOGUE\n[02]\nARCHIVE SELECTION\n\nSPOTLIGHT SELECTION\n\n1990 Pinstripe Double-Breasted Jacket\nRegular price\n$1,500.00\nSOLD OUT\n\nSARTORIAL ARCHIVE\n\n1999 Technical Cotton Trench\nRegular price\n$1,690.00\n\nSARTORIAL ARCHIVE\n\n1998 Bias-Cut Silk Evening Slip\nRegular price\n$1,450.00\n01 / 02\nVIEW ALL CURRENT CATALOGUE\n\nPLATE V / CONSERVATION STUDY\n\nThree objects from the archive record\n\nEach piece is examined under raking light, stabilized by our conservationist, and released in small curated entries.\n\n1\n2\n3\n\nGarment study room photographed under raking light.\n\n1990 Pinstripe Double-Breasted Jacket\nRegular price\n$1,500.00\nSOLD OUT\nCondition: Restored\nRestored\n×\nOption unavailable\nSize: FR 40 / US 8\nFR 40 / US 8\n×\nOption unavailable\nQuantity\nSOLD OUT\nSold out\n\nClimate-controlled archival transport | Insured courier\n\nNarrow chalk stripes run across a structured wool jacket with a peaked lapel and six-button front. Masterfully conserved under Record AR-1990-01. Single historical piece, 1 of 1.\n\nCATALOGUE NOTICES\n\nNew entries in the archive\n\nOccasional notices of restored objects, new records and workshop visits.\n\nEmail address\nSUBSCRIBE\nSartorial Archive\n\nPRIVATE CORRESPONDENCE\n\nNotes from the studio\n\nNew objects, material studies and private previews, sent with restraint.\n\nEmail address\nSUBSCRIBE\nSearch\nRefund policy\nShipping policy\nPrivacy policy\nTerms of service\nContact information\nAccepted payment methods\n© 2026 Sartorial Archive\nPowered by Shopify",
